;   project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_animated_animals.tres.
; Display name "Shiba Inu"; id/directory use `shiba_inu` (content-pipeline-status.md).
;
; SPECIES: domestic dog, Shiba Inu breed (Canis lupus familiaris).
;
; AVOIDS: ruled in as row 9's second Avoids pair (D-43) — mutual and symmetric with Husky.
; Both are domestic dogs, so the structural predation-graph check stays clean the same way
; it does for Rabbit <-> Fox. Personality split (Husky Bold, Shiba Inu Shy) matches each
; breed's documented real temperament (huskies outgoing/pack-social, Shiba Inu independent/
; reserved) and gives this second pair its own visibility hook.
;
; CAPACITY FIELDS (D-43): capacity_radius = 0 -> SENTINEL `CAPACITY_RADIUS_FOLLOWS_SCOUT`,
; meaning "equal to scout_radius" (8), not a radius of zero. tiles_per_individual = 2,
; max_individuals = 6. Farm-tolerant, "village dog" — house + open_grass habitat.
;
; fact_text: NO CLEARED COPY EXISTS. docs/content/cleared-pool-fact-cards.md § Shiba Inu
; ran the full four-approved-source search (ADW's general Canis lupus familiaris account
; never names Shiba Inu; Nat Geo Kids has no breed page for either dog in this pool; Nat
; Geo Society Education turned up nothing breed-specific; a widely repeated "most wolf-like
; genetically" claim traces to no locatable primary source on either approved NatGeo domain)
; and explicitly declined to fabricate or ship a weak substitute — D-43 records this as
; "not ruled on here". Per this dispatch's brief, `fact_text` is set to the required
; PLACEHOLDER form so validate() reports a known, correctly-flagged gap rather than a
; silent empty string. DO NOT invent a fact here — replace only once step 1/5 clears a
; real source.
;
; news_reports intentionally empty — News Report pools for this pool are a separate, later
; purchase (not part of Content Pipeline step 4/5 for this dispatch).
